---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import Sidebar from '../components/Sidebar.astro'
---

<DocsLayout title="Theming">
  <Sidebar slot="sidebar" />

  <article class="docs-content">
    <h1>Theming</h1>

    <h2>CSS Custom Properties</h2>
    <p>Semantic UI React v4 uses CSS custom properties (variables) for all design tokens. Override them to customize the look:</p>
    <pre><code>{`:root {
  --sui-color-primary: #2185d0;
  --sui-color-secondary: #1b1c1d;
  --sui-font-family: Lato, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
  --sui-border-radius: 0.28571429rem;
}`}</code></pre>

    <h2>ThemeProvider</h2>
    <p>Use the ThemeProvider component for scoped theming:</p>
    <pre><code>{`import { ThemeProvider } from 'semantic-ui-react'

<ThemeProvider theme="dark">
  <App />
</ThemeProvider>`}</code></pre>

    <h2>Dark Theme</h2>
    <p>Import the built-in dark theme:</p>
    <pre><code>{`import 'semantic-ui-react/styles/themes/dark.css'`}</code></pre>

    <h2>Custom Themes</h2>
    <p>Create a custom theme by overriding CSS custom properties:</p>
    <pre><code>{`.my-theme {
  --sui-color-primary: #e03997;
  --sui-color-background: #f5f5f5;
  --sui-color-text: #333;
}`}</code></pre>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
